Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:22:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] OrionLayer Open Fix 111: the colony screen's demolish,
 addressed by id (MSG_DEMOLISH 0x8C: int16 colony, int16 building;
 CAP_DEMOLISH 0x0002 in HELLO_REPLY. On SCREEN_COLONY, for the colony on
 screen and the player's, outside the planet view, a building it has: the
 satellite slot first, as Evaluate_Input asks satellites first
 (colony.cpp:1323-1324), else the first cell of Check_Bldg_Fields' own walk
 that holds it, is activated as MSG_ACTIVATE does; for a cell
 ext::Take_Demolish_Field makes the walk read that field as the scanned one
 and the pointer as on no polygon, so the hidden window's pointer cannot claim
 the click at an earlier cell (:1999-2011). The rest is the original's,
 unchanged: the buildings it ignores, the once-a-turn refusal (E 0x243), the
 confirmation (E 0x107) in the colony screen's own loop, reaching a client as
 MSGB, the rubble, the removal, the recalculation, the refund)

OrionLayer, open fix 111.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
